# .easignore — controls what gets uploaded to EAS Build.
#
# THIS FILE MUST LIVE AT THE REPO ROOT. EAS archives the whole git repository
# and builds from the `notes-app` subdirectory, so the ignore file is read from
# — and every pattern is matched against — the repo root, not notes-app/.
# A copy inside notes-app/ is read by nothing; the August 2026 build failure
# below is what that looks like.
#
# When present, this file REPLACES .gitignore for the EAS upload, so it must
# list everything that should be excluded, including things git already ignores.
# Verify a change with:
#   cd notes-app && npx eas build:inspect -p android --stage archive --output <dir>

# Native projects: this is a CNG/managed app. EAS runs `expo prebuild` on the
# server to regenerate android/ and ios/ with correct Linux paths. Uploading the
# local (Windows) native folders ships build output holding hardcoded D:\ paths;
# Gradle then resolved a module to
# `.../build/notes-app/android/D:/dev2/w_notes/notes-app/node_modules/...` and
# the build died at configuration time.
notes-app/android/
notes-app/ios/

# Dependencies (reinstalled on the builder)
node_modules/

# Expo / Metro / build output
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts
.metro-health-check*

# Logs & debug
*.log
crash.txt
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
maestro-artifacts/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Local env & secrets. Builds use remote (Expo-hosted) credentials, so the local
# keystore and the credentials.json pointing at it never need to be uploaded.
.env
.env*.local
credentials.json
credentials/
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
*.pem

# Editor / OS cruft
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
*.orig.*

# Local tooling and agent worktrees (each worktree is a second checkout of this
# same repo — uploading them doubles the archive)
.claude/
.githooks/
local/
example

# Sibling projects: the Android app build reads none of these
backend/
terraform/
logo/
.github/
